<div id="2026-09-03-dryer-plan-conflict-resolved" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-03 — DryerProjectPlan.tt merge conflict resolved (plus root cause of the empty queue)</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> <code>Documentation/DryerProjectPlan.tt</code> had unresolved conflict markers at lines 38/49/63 (<code>&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;</code> / <code>=======</code> / <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;</code>), so the main dryer hub was rendering broken. Resolved by keeping the accurate content from <em>both</em> sides rather than picking one.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Kept from "Updated upstream":</strong> the make-or-buy note, the <code>/Inventory/invoice/new</code> receive path, the warning that printed parts stored as <code>item_origin=purchased</code> will be treated as buy-not-print, and the "do not queue a job named Module 1.3mf" rule (this last line had been orphaned below the conflict).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Kept from "Stashed changes":</strong> the corrected BOM description (one of each *01 and *02 per unit), the Browse Inventory/Order split, and the picture/<code>image_path</code> note.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Added — root cause of the empty queue.</strong> Measured while merging: the base (52) and add-on (53) BOMs carry <b>70 components marked <code>item_origin=purchased</code></b> against only <b>15 marked <code>3d_printed</code></b>. Most of the 70 are genuinely printed parts (corners, side panels, doors, spool brackets). That is why the print queue never filled from the BOM and why <code>/3d/queue_sync</code> reports nothing needed — sync compares against BOM lines, and the BOM says those parts are bought. Correcting <code>item_origin</code> is a prerequisite for a trustworthy queue and is now the first item under "Next".</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Also noted:</strong> #2310 PO-R1 is <em>in progress</em> (status 2), and 94 items on sitename=3d lack <code>image_path</code> even though 3MF <code>top_N.png</code> previews exist.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Verified.</strong> Zero conflict markers remain in the file; template renders (75 KB) with the new content present.</p>
</div>
